  "slug": "sequences-promoter-38cf",
  "summary": "AlphaFold 3 accuracy drops on novel RNA folds, prompting validation of deep-learning RNA predictions against deposited structures.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational prediction and assessment of RNA structure. ScanFold3 accelerates secondary structure scanning for structured RNA targets in genomes and transcriptomes, reporting 38-129x gains over ScanFold2. A conkit-validate extension to RNA compares contact patterns from deep-learning predictors against deposited structures. AlphaFold 3, evaluated on over 1,300 protein-RNA complexes and about 270 RNA-only systems, shows fold and interface accuracy declining on novel RNAs. CryoID2 applies 3D U-Net analysis to cryoEM maps to identify RNA and protein candidates. Struct-Caliper and the ProteinMPNN-based proteome recoding study address protein structure search and sequence design, respectively, and are adjacent rather than central. What is new is testing deep-learning RNA predictions against experimental structures and novel folds, not only generating them.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-05"
}
